After the upgraded Reception read-only smoke check, the WSL test environment
lost the managed bench listeners and regenerated /etc/hosts without the local
site aliases. The first failed-asset HTTP observation ended in DNS resolution
error; it is not counted as the expected controlled HTTP 404 gate.

Live handles 69923 and 12558 were polled to terminal exit 0. Their receipts show
the post-UI baseline comparison and then the deliberately injected asset fault.
Both helper invocations had been launched before the first was observed terminal;
the fault invocation retained its probe/fault state and private asset payload,
but replaced the in-memory check journal entry of the concurrent observer.
The public comparison receipt remains preserved. An exclusive process lock was
added to serialize subsequent rehearsal helper actions. No business action is
repeated to repair that observation metadata.

